    "body": "> > How does this work in terms of callbacks and such? The prior approach was that the algorithm would return a response. I'm not entirely sure that was workable, but I'm not sure what the new approach is.\r\n> \r\n> The new approach is reviewable here: [whatwg/html#8097](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/8097)\r\n\r\nSpecifically, we don't need new callbacks because we don't replace `fetch params`. `process response` etc still work the same way, the only thing that changes is that instead of processing redirects automatically we have to call `next` from the outside.",
