    "updated_at": "2022-09-26T15:03:17Z",
    "body": "> \"process response\" is an argument of the fetch algorithm, not something you can wait for.\r\n\r\nThis was there in the HTML spec before and I didn't care to refactor it here... but I can if it makes a difference - perhaps `process the next redirect` can pass a new callback if it's more readable, but the behavior would be the same.",
